6_mean: 0.747\n      high_6_std: 0.01\n      mid_8_mean: 0.706\n      mid_8_std: 0.013\n      low_5_mean: 0.601\n      low_5_std: 0.029\n      all_19_mean: 0.691\n    - layer: L40\n      high_6_mean: 0.753\n      high_6_std: 0.01\n      mid_8_mean: 0.711\n      mid_8_std: 0.013\n      low_5_mean: 0.607\n      low_5_std: 0.032\n      all_19_mean: 0.696\n    - layer: L52\n      high_6_mean: 0.741\n      high_6_std: 0.011\n      mid_8_mean: 0.697\n      mid_8_std: 0.015\n      low_5_mean: 0.586\n      low_5_std: 0.035\n      all_19_mean: 0.682\n    - layer: L64\n      high_6_mean: 0.721\n      high_6_std: 0.013\n      mid_8_mean: 0.673\n      mid_8_std: 0.017\n      low_5_mean: 0.558\n      low_5_std: 0.039\n      all_19_mean: 0.661\n    - layer: L76\n      high_6_mean: 0.705\n      high_6_std: 0.01\n      mid_8_mean: 0.657\n      mid_8_std: 0.016\n      low_5_mean: 0.54\n      low_5_std: 0.033\n      all_19_mean: 0.644\n    - layer: L92\n      high_6_mean: 0.672\n      high_6_std: 0.015\n      mid_8_mean: 0.621\n      mid_8_std: 0.02\n      low_5_mean: 0.497\n      low_5_std: 0.042\n      all_19_mean: 0.607\n  - title: Per-Language Zero-Shot AUROC at L40 (Best Transfer) and L76 (Best English)\n    columns:\n    - lang\n    - tier\n    - L40_auroc\n    - L76_auroc\n    - delta_pp\n    data:\n    - lang: zh\n      tier: high\n      L40_auroc: 0.762\n      L76_auroc: 0.712\n      delta_pp: -5.0\n    - lang: de\n      tier: high\n      L40_auroc: 0.753\n      L76_auroc: 0.703\n      delta_pp: -5.0\n    - lang: fr\n      tier: high\n      L40_auroc: 0.757\n      L76_auroc: 0.708\n      delta_pp: -4.9\n    - lang: es\n      tier: high\n      L40_auroc: 0.764\n      L76_auroc: 0.715\n      delta_pp: -4.9\n    - lang: ja\n      tier: high\n      L40_auroc: 0.737\n      L76_auroc: 0.688\n      delta_pp: -4.9\n    - lang: ru\n      tier: high\n      L40_auroc: 0.744\n      L76_auroc: 0.697\n      delta_pp: -4.7\n    - lang: ar\n      tier: mid\n      L40_auroc: 0.717\n      L76_auroc: 0.667\n      delta_pp: -5.0\n    - lang: hi\n      tier: mid\n      L40_auroc: 0.71\n      L76_auroc: 0.659\n      delta_pp: -5.1\n    - lang: ko\n      tier: mid\n      L40_auroc: 0.703\n      L76_auroc: 0.652\n      delta_pp: -5.1\n    - lang: pt\n      tier: mid\n      L40_auroc: 0.731\n      L76_auroc: 0.681\n      delta_pp: -5.0\n    - lang: vi\n      tier: mid\n      L40_auroc: 0.696\n      L76_auroc: 0.644\n      delta_pp: -5.2\n    - lang: th\n      tier: mid\n      L40_auroc: 0.688\n      L76_auroc: 0.633\n      delta_pp: -5.5\n    - lang: tr\n      tier: mid\n      L40_auroc: 0.706\n      L76_auroc: 0.655\n      delta_pp: -5.1\n    - lang: pl\n      tier: mid\n      L40_auroc: 0.723\n      L76_auroc: 0.673\n      delta_pp: -5.0\n    - lang: sw\n      tier: low\n      L40_auroc: 0.638\n      L76_auroc: 0.579\n      delta_pp: -5.9\n    - lang: te\n      tier: low\n      L40_auroc: 0.644\n      L76_auroc: 0.59\n      delta_pp: -5.4\n    - lang: my\n      tier: low\n      L40_auroc: 0.607\n      L76_auroc: 0.543\n      delta_pp: -6.4\n    - lang: am\n      tier: low\n      L40_auroc: 0.583\n      L76_auroc: 0.532\n      delta_pp: -5.1\n    - lang: yo\n      tier: low\n      L40_auroc: 0.561\n      L76_auroc: 0.51\n      delta_pp: -5.1\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Figure 1a: Pareto frontier scatter — x-axis: English AUROC, y-axis: zero-shot\n    transfer mean AUROC (19 langs). Each point is one probed layer (L0–L92), color-coded\n    by depth percentage. Clear upward-then-left curve: shallow layers cluster at bottom-left\n    (both low), mid layers at upper-right of transfer axis (L40 peak), deep layers\n    drift right on English axis but downward on transfer. Pareto-efficient frontier\n    connects L40→L48→L56→L64→L76. Annotate L40 (\"best transfer\") and L76 (\"best English\").\n\n    '\n  - 'Figure 1b: Layer-depth profile — dual y-axis plot. Left axis: English AUROC (blue,\n    rising then plateau). Right axis: ZS transfer mean (orange, rising then falling).\n    Crossover region around L44–L52 clearly visible. Shaded band shows ±1σ across\n    19 languages on the transfer curve — band widens at deeper layers.\n\n    '\n  - 'Figure 1c: Heatmap — rows: 19 languages (grouped by resource tier), columns:\n    24 layers. Cell color: zero-shot AUROC. Clear gradient: high-resource rows are\n    warm (0.65–0.76) across most layers; low-resource rows are cool (0.50–0.64) with\n    the warm zone concentrated at mid-depth layers. Visual pattern immediately shows\n    depth-transferability × resource interaction.\n\n    '\n  analysis: 'Qwen3-235B exhibits a textbook Pareto frontier for Claim 1. The depth-transferability\n    tradeoff is sharp: 36 layers separate the best-EN (L76) and best-transfer (L40)\n    operating points, with 16.8pp transfer degradation at L76. The layer ranking consistency\n    ρ=0.71 means 19 languages broadly agree on which depths transfer best, supporting\n    the claim that this is a structural property of the model rather than a language-specific\n    artifact. Low-resource languages show the expected fragility: 3/5 pass but am\n    and yo fall below the 0.60 AUROC threshold even at the optimal transfer layer.\n    This will be framed as a resource-tier modulation of the Pareto frontier rather\n    than a failure of the phenomenon. Mean-shift''s continued failure (replicating\n    MVP) cleanly motivates CaCLR.\n\n    '\n- name: Full Pareto Frontier — Llama 4 Scout\n  plan_id: plan_002\n  description: '48-layer MoE model, INT8 quantization. 12 probed layers (every 4th:\n    L0–L44). 20 languages, 5 transfer conditions. Second architecture for cross-model\n    Pareto frontier comparison (Claim 1).\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    en_auroc_best: 0.793\n    en_best_layer: L44\n    en_auroc_range:\n    - 0.538\n    - 0.793\n    en_ece_raw_at_best: 0.178\n    en_ece_tempcal_at_best: 0.063\n    temp_scaling_T: 5.41\n    zs_transfer_auroc_mean_19lang_at_best_en: 0.657\n    zs_transfer_drop_at_best_en_pp: 13.6\n    best_transfer_layer: L32\n    zs_transfer_auroc_mean_at_best_transfer: 0.679\n    en_auroc_at_best_transfer: 0.771\n    pareto_depth_transfer_rank_corr: 0.56\n    low_resource_zs_pass_rate: 0.4\n    mean_shift_improvement_rate: 0.05\n    linproj_auroc_mean_at_best_transfer: 0.705\n    pareto_frontier_agreement_with_qwen3: 0.67\n  result_rationale: 'Llama 4 Scout 仅 48 层（vs Qwen3 的 94 层），Pareto 前沿更 flat/noisy。\n    英语 AUROC 峰值 0.793 低于 Qwen3 的 0.812，原因是 Scout 作为 MoE 的 active 参数量（~17B）小于 Qwen3-A22B，correctness\n    信号的 linear accessibility 稍弱。 最佳迁移层 L32（67% 深度）vs 最佳英语层 L44（92% 深度）仅相隔 12 层，前沿\n    更紧凑。Transfer drop 13.6pp 低于 Qwen3 的 16.8pp，说明 Llama4 的深层 representation language-specificity\n    增长更平缓——可能与 Llama4 的训练数据分布有关（更多多语言 数据在预训练中）。跨语言层序一致性 ρ=0.56 明显低于 Qwen3 的 0.71，表明不同\n    语言在 Llama4 上对最优迁移层的偏好更分散，Pareto 结构存在但更 noisy。 与 Qwen3 的 frontier agreement 0.67\n    说明两个架构共享定性趋势（\"中层比深层 迁移更好\"）但定量最优点不同——这正是 \"architecture-dependent\" claim 的证据。 低资源仅\n    2/5 通过，sw 和 te 勉强过线，my/am/yo 失败。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - title: English AUROC by Layer (Logistic Regression)\n    columns:\n    - layer\n    - depth_pct\n    - en_auroc\n    - en_ece_raw\n    data:\n    - layer: L0\n      depth_pct: 0\n      en_auroc: 0.538\n      en_ece_raw: 0.336\n    - layer: L4\n      depth_pct: 8\n      en_auroc: 0.571\n      en_ece_raw: 0.318\n    - layer: L8\n      depth_pct: 17\n      en_auroc: 0.613\n      en_ece_raw: 0.296\n    - layer: L12\n      depth_pct: 25\n      en_auroc: 0.651\n      en_ece_raw: 0.272\n    - layer: L16\n      depth_pct: 33\n      en_auroc: 0.688\n      en_ece_raw: 0.248\n    - layer: L20\n      depth_pct: 42\n      en_auroc: 0.718\n      en_ece_raw: 0.228\n    - layer: L24\n      depth_pct: 50\n      en_auroc: 0.741\n      en_ece_raw: 0.212\n    - layer: L28\n      depth_pct: 58\n      en_auroc: 0.759\n      en_ece_raw: 0.199\n    - layer: L32\n      depth_pct: 67\n      en_auroc: 0.771\n      en_ece_raw: 0.19\n    - layer: L36\n      depth_pct: 75\n      en_auroc: 0.782\n      en_ece_raw: 0.183\n    - layer: L40\n      depth_pct: 83\n      en_auroc: 0.79\n      en_ece_raw: 0.179\n    - layer: L44\n      depth_pct: 92\n      en_auroc: 0.793\n      en_ece_raw: 0.178\n  - title: Zero-Shot Transfer AUROC by Resource Tier\n    columns:\n    - layer\n    - high_6_mean\n    - mid_8_mean\n    - low_5_mean\n    - all_19_mean\n    data:\n    - layer: L16\n      high_6_mean: 0.713\n      mid_8_mean: 0.67\n      low_5_mean: 0.571\n      all_19_mean: 0.659\n    - layer: L24\n      high_6_mean: 0.731\n      mid_8_mean: 0.691\n      low_5_mean: 0.587\n      all_19_mean: 0.677\n    - layer: L28\n      high_6_mean: 0.737\n      mid_8_mean: 0.697\n      low_5_mean: 0.591\n      all_19_mean: 0.683\n    - layer: L32\n      high_6_mean: 0.738\n      mid_8_mean: 0.694\n      low_5_mean: 0.585\n      all_19_mean: 0.679\n    - layer: L36\n      high_6_mean: 0.733\n      mid_8_mean: 0.688\n      low_5_mean: 0.574\n      all_19_mean: 0.673\n    - layer: L40\n      high_6_mean: 0.724\n      mid_8_mean: 0.678\n      low_5_mean: 0.561\n      all_19_mean: 0.663\n    - layer: L44\n      high_6_mean: 0.714\n      mid_8_mean: 0.669\n      low_5_mean: 0.548\n      all_19_mean: 0.657\n  - title: Cross-Architecture Pareto Comparison\n    columns:\n    - metric\n    - qwen3_235b\n    - llama4_scout\n    - interpretation\n    data:\n    - metric: en_auroc_best\n      qwen3_235b: 0.812\n      llama4_scout: 0.793\n      interpretation: Qwen3 higher, more layers for correctness to accumulate\n    - metric: best_transfer_depth_pct\n      qwen3_235b: 43\n      llama4_scout: 67\n      interpretation: Llama4 optimal transfer much deeper (flatter frontier)\n    - metric: zs_drop_at_best_en_pp\n      qwen3_235b: 16.8\n      llama4_scout: 13.6\n      interpretation: Qwen3 sharper tradeoff, Llama4 flatter\n    - metric: layer_rank_consistency\n      qwen3_235b: 0.71\n      llama4_scout: 0.56\n      interpretation: Qwen3 more consistent across languages\n    - metric: frontier_gap_layers\n      qwen3_235b: 36\n      llama4_scout: 12\n      interpretation: Qwen3 has wider Pareto gap\n    - metric: frontier_agreement\n      qwen3_235b: null\n      llama4_scout: null\n      interpretation: Spearman ρ=0.67 across 19 langs\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Figure 2: Overlaid Pareto frontiers for Qwen3 (circles) and Llama4 (triangles)\n    on same axes (EN AUROC × ZS transfer mean). Qwen3 frontier is wider and steeper;\n    Llama4 is more compact and flatter. Annotated inset: depth percentage labels show\n    Qwen3''s optimal transfer at 43% depth vs Llama4 at 67% depth — architecture-dependent\n    optimal operating point. This is the main Figure 1 of the paper.\n\n    '\n  analysis: 'Llama 4 Scout 确认 Pareto frontier 的跨架构泛化性，但 frontier shape 明显不同： 更 flat、更\n    compact、更 noisy。这支持 Claim 1 的 \"architecture-dependent\" 修饰语。 关键对比：Qwen3 的最优迁移在\n    43% 深度，Llama4 在 67% 深度——practitioners 不能 假设一个固定的 \"最优层百分比\"。Llama4 较低的层序一致性（0.56\n    vs 0.71）暗示 其内部 multilingual representation 的组织方式更分散，可能与 Scout 的 MoE routing 策略有关。两架构的\n    frontier agreement 0.67 说明定性趋势共享但定量不可直接迁移。\n\n    '\n- name: CaCLR Implementation and Comparative Evaluation\n  plan_id: plan_003\n  description: 'L_CaCLR = L_BCE + α·L_SB-ECE + β·L_consistency. Trained using English\n    correctness labels + unlabeled parallel activations from 19 target languages.\n    Hyperparameter sweep: α∈{0.1,0.2,0.3,0.5,1.0}, β∈{0.05,0.1,0.15,0.2,0.3}. Compared\n    against 4 baselines across full Pareto frontier for both models × 20 languages.\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    best_alpha: 0.3\n    best_beta: 0.15\n    qwen3_L40_caclr_auroc_mean: 0.738\n    qwen3_L40_caclr_ece_mean: 0.112\n    qwen3_L40_linproj_auroc_mean: 0.724\n    qwen3_L40_zeroshot_auroc_mean: 0.696\n    qwen3_L40_caclr_vs_linproj_pp: 1.4\n    qwen3_L76_caclr_auroc_mean: 0.695\n    qwen3_L76_linproj_auroc_mean: 0.678\n    qwen3_L76_caclr_vs_linproj_pp: 1.7\n    llama4_L32_caclr_auroc_mean: 0.717\n    llama4_L32_linproj_auroc_mean: 0.705\n    llama4_L32_caclr_vs_linproj_pp: 1.2\n    caclr_vs_linproj_auroc_delta_mean_pp: 1.3\n    caclr_ece_reduction_vs_tempcal_pct: 21.1\n    caclr_improvement_over_zs_pass_rate: 0.89\n    caclr_improvement_over_linproj_pass_rate: 0.74\n    qwen3_caclr_optimal_layer: L52\n    qwen3_zs_optimal_layer: L40\n    qwen3_frontier_shift_layers: 12\n    llama4_caclr_optimal_layer: L36\n    llama4_zs_optimal_layer: L32\n    llama4_frontier_shift_layers: 4\n    caclr_fails_vs_linproj_langs:\n    - th\n    - my\n    - am\n    - yo\n    - te\n    mean_shift_any_improvement: 1\n  result_rationale: 'CaCLR 在 median 档位下表现为 \"matches or marginally exceeds linear projection\"。\n    核心原因：consistency term（L_consistency）对齐的是 unlabeled parallel activations 的 probe\n    output distribution，在中-高资源语言中有效（parallel corpus 质量好， 激活空间足够对齐），但在低资源语言中由于 (a)\n    GlobalMMLU 翻译噪声 (b) tokenizer 覆盖率低导致 activation 本身质量差，consistency 信号变成噪声。因此 CaCLR\n    比 zero-shot 有显著改善（+4.2pp at L40），但比 linear projection 仅高 1.3pp 平均—— 因为 linear\n    projection 已经利用了 target-language activations 做对齐。CaCLR 的 真正优势在 Pareto shift：它把最优工作层从\n    L40 推到 L52（Qwen3），在更深层维持 迁移质量，同时获得 +2.0pp 英语 AUROC。SB-ECE loss 使 CaCLR probe 自带\n    calibration， ECE 比 temperature-scaled zero-shot 低 21.1%——这是方法论层面的 practical benefit。\n    Hyperparameter 敏感度中等：α=0.3 在 0.2-0.5 范围内差异小于 0.5pp，β 更敏感—— β>0.2 时 consistency\n    过强导致英语 AUROC 下降。5 个失败语言（th/my/am/yo/te） 中 4 个是低资源或 activation 质量低的语言，th 是 mid-resource\n    但独特的声调语言 导致 alignment 困难。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - title: 5-Method Comparison at Qwen3-235B Pareto-Optimal Layer (L40)\n    columns:\n    - method\n    - auroc_mean\n    - auroc_high\n    - auroc_mid\n    - auroc_low\n    - ece_mean\n    - brier_mean\n    data:\n    - method: zero-shot\n      auroc_mean: 0.696\n      auroc_high: 0.753\n      auroc_mid: 0.711\n      auroc_low: 0.607\n      ece_mean: 0.148\n      brier_mean: 0.286\n    - method: mean-shift\n      auroc_mean: 0.683\n      auroc_high: 0.742\n      auroc_mid: 0.698\n      auroc_low: 0.591\n      ece_mean: 0.155\n      brier_mean: 0.294\n    - method: linear-proj\n      auroc_mean: 0.724\n      auroc_high: 0.775\n      auroc_mid: 0.738\n      auroc_low: 0.633\n      ece_mean: 0.121\n      brier_mean: 0.261\n    - method: few-shot-25\n      auroc_mean: 0.711\n      auroc_high: 0.766\n      auroc_mid: 0.725\n      auroc_low: 0.618\n      ece_mean: 0.132\n      brier_mean: 0.27\n    - method: few-shot-100\n      auroc_mean: 0.743\n      auroc_high: 0.791\n      auroc_mid: 0.756\n      auroc_low: 0.655\n      ece_mean: 0.108\n      brier_mean: 0.247\n    - method: CaCLR\n      auroc_mean: 0.738\n      auroc_high: 0.786\n      auroc_mid: 0.754\n      auroc_low: 0.636\n      ece_mean: 0.112\n      brier_mean: 0.251\n  - title: 5-Method Comparison at Llama 4 Scout L32\n    columns:\n    - method\n    - auroc_mean\n    - auroc_high\n    - auroc_mid\n    - auroc_low\n    - ece_mean\n    data:\n    - method: zero-shot\n      auroc_mean: 0.679\n      auroc_high: 0.738\n      auroc_mid: 0.694\n      auroc_low: 0.585\n      ece_mean: 0.153\n    - method: mean-shift\n      auroc_mean: 0.668\n      auroc_high: 0.726\n      auroc_mid: 0.682\n      auroc_low: 0.577\n      ece_mean: 0.161\n    - method: linear-proj\n      auroc_mean: 0.705\n      auroc_high: 0.758\n      auroc_mid: 0.72\n      auroc_low: 0.61\n      ece_mean: 0.129\n    - method: few-shot-25\n      auroc_mean: 0.694\n      auroc_high: 0.749\n      auroc_mid: 0.708\n      auroc_low: 0.602\n      ece_mean: 0.138\n    - method: few-shot-100\n      auroc_mean: 0.728\n      auroc_high: 0.776\n      auroc_mid: 0.741\n      auroc_low: 0.64\n      ece_mean: 0.113\n    - method: CaCLR\n      auroc_mean: 0.717\n      auroc_high: 0.769\n      auroc_mid: 0.733\n      auroc_low: 0.618\n      ece_mean: 0.122\n  - title: CaCLR vs Linear Projection per Resource Tier (Qwen3, averaged across Pareto\n      layers)\n    columns:\n    - tier\n    - n_langs\n    - caclr_auroc\n    - linproj_auroc\n    - delta_pp\n    - caclr_wins\n    data:\n    - tier: high\n      n_langs: 6\n      caclr_auroc: 0.786\n      linproj_auroc: 0.775\n      delta_pp: 1.1\n      caclr_wins: 6/6\n    - tier: mid\n      n_langs: 8\n      caclr_auroc: 0.754\n      linproj_auroc: 0.738\n      delta_pp: 1.6\n      caclr_wins: 7/8\n    - tier: low\n      n_langs: 5\n      caclr_auroc: 0.636\n      linproj_auroc: 0.633\n      delta_pp: 0.3\n      caclr_wins: 1/5\n  - title: CaCLR Consistency Term Ablation (Qwen3 L52)\n    note: α=0.30 fixed; β=0 is calibrated-only probe\n    columns:\n    - config\n    - auroc_mean\n    - ece_mean\n    - high_delta_vs_linproj\n    - mid_delta_vs_linproj\n    - low_delta_vs_linproj\n    data:\n    - config: α=0.3 β=0 (no consistency)\n      auroc_mean: 0.716\n      ece_mean: 0.119\n      high_delta_vs_linproj: 0.3\n      mid_delta_vs_linproj: -0.2\n      low_delta_vs_linproj: -0.5\n    - config: α=0.3 β=0.15 (full CaCLR)\n      auroc_mean: 0.733\n      ece_mean: 0.112\n      high_delta_vs_linproj: 0.8\n      mid_delta_vs_linproj: 1.4\n      low_delta_vs_linproj: -0.2\n    - config: α=0 β=0.15 (consistency only)\n      auroc_mean: 0.708\n      ece_mean: 0.136\n      high_delta_vs_linproj: -0.4\n      mid_delta_vs_linproj: 0.6\n      low_delta_vs_linproj: -0.8\n  - title: Hyperparameter Sensitivity (Qwen3, validation set mean AUROC across 5 langs)\n    columns:\n    - alpha\n    - beta_0.05\n    - beta_0.10\n    - beta_0.15\n    - beta_0.20\n    - beta_0.30\n    data:\n    - alpha: 0.1\n      beta_0.05: 0.704\n      beta_0.10: 0.709\n      beta_0.15: 0.711\n      beta_0.20: 0.708\n      beta_0.30: 0.699\n    - alpha: 0.2\n      beta_0.05: 0.711\n      beta_0.10: 0.718\n      beta_0.15: 0.724\n      beta_0.20: 0.72\n      beta_0.30: 0.708\n    - alpha: 0.3\n      beta_0.05: 0.715\n      beta_0.10: 0.723\n      beta_0.15: 0.731\n      beta_0.20: 0.726\n      beta_0.30: 0.712\n    - alpha: 0.5\n      beta_0.05: 0.712\n      beta_0.10: 0.719\n      beta_0.15: 0.725\n      beta_0.20: 0.718\n      beta_0.30: 0.701\n    - alpha: 1.0\n      beta_0.05: 0.698\n      beta_0.10: 0.703\n      beta_0.15: 0.706\n      beta_0.20: 0.695\n      beta_0.30: 0.674\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Figure 3a: Pareto frontier shift — overlaid zero-shot frontier (grey) and CaCLR\n    frontier (blue) for Qwen3. CaCLR frontier is shifted up-and-right: at the same\n    English AUROC, CaCLR achieves higher transfer; at the same transfer quality, CaCLR\n    operates at deeper layers. Annotated: zero-shot optimal (L40) vs CaCLR optimal\n    (L52), with arrows showing +2.0pp English gain and +1.2pp transfer gain.\n\n    '\n  - 'Figure 3b: Bar chart — CaCLR AUROC improvement over linear projection, grouped\n    by resource tier. High-resource bars around +1.1pp (all positive). Mid-resource\n    bars around +1.6pp (7/8 positive, th near zero). Low-resource bars around +0.3pp\n    (mostly near zero or negative). Clear visual: CaCLR''s consistency term primarily\n    benefits mid-resource languages.\n\n    '\n  - 'Figure 3c: ECE comparison — grouped bar chart with 5 methods × 3 resource tiers.\n    CaCLR ECE bars consistently among the lowest, comparable to few-shot-100 for high/mid\n    resource but without requiring any target-language labels.\n\n    '\n  analysis: 'CaCLR 的 median-tier 表现支持 \"zero-label alternative that matches supervised\n    transfer\" 的 framing，而非 \"大幅超越\" 的 framing。核心发现：(1) CaCLR 在 zero-label 设定下 接近 few-shot-100\n    的性能（差 0.5pp AUROC，差 0.4pp ECE），这是 practical value 的 来源；(2) vs linear projection\n    仅 +1.3pp，但 CaCLR 不需要任何 target-language 数据 结构假设（linear projection 假设线性可分对齐），是更\n    principled 的方案；(3) consistency term 的 ablation 清晰显示其主要贡献在 mid-resource 语言（+1.6pp），\n    这些语言有足够好的 parallel activation 质量让 consistency loss 有效，但又不像 high-resource 那样 zero-shot\n    已经很好。Paper 应将 CaCLR 定位为 \"practical tool for the mid-resource sweet spot\" 而非 universal\n    improvement。\n\n    '\n- name: Difficulty-Controlled Ablation\n  plan_id: plan_004\n  description: 'IRT difficulty probes (Ridge regression on human difficulty scores\n    per Civelli et al.) trained per layer, difficulty direction projected out of activations,\n    correctness probes retrained on residuals, transfer evaluated. 10 languages ×\n    8 layers per model.\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    difficulty_probe_en_R2_mean: 0.68\n    difficulty_probe_zs_R2_mean: 0.61\n    decomp_difficulty_var_explained_pct: 37\n    original_transfer_gap_pp: 15.2\n    residual_transfer_gap_pp: 11.4\n    gap_reduction_pp: 3.8\n    gap_reduction_pct: 25\n    residual_en_auroc_drop: 0.038\n    language_family_cluster_effect: IE languages (de/fr/es/pl/ru) cluster; others\n      scattered\n    capability_residual_noisy: true\n    prescriptive_accuracy: 0.72\n  result_rationale: 'Difficulty 是已知的跨语言可迁移特征（Civelli et al. 直接证明了 IRT difficulty probe\n    的跨语言迁移性）。在 median 档，difficulty 解释了 correctness direction 37% 的方差， 因为 \"题目难不难\" 确实是\n    correctness 的一个强组成部分（简单题各语言都对，难题各 语言都错）。但 correctness 还包含 \"模型在该语言上是否具备回答这道题的 capability\"\n    这一 language-dependent 成分。投影掉 difficulty 后，transfer gap 从 15.2pp 缩小到 11.4pp（减少\n    25%），比 variance-explained 的 37% 低是因为 projection 是线性的而 difficulty-correctness 的关系有非线性成分。残差中的\n    capability-specific 信号是 noisy 的：高资源语言表现出清晰的 language-family clustering（IE 语言的\n    capability profiles 相似），但低资源语言的 capability residual 被 tokenization 和数据质量 confound，\n    无法干净分离。Prescriptive accuracy 72% 意味着：当 decomposition 预测 \"这个 language-layer 对简单\n    baseline 就够了\" 时，72% 的情况下确实如此——有用但不完美。 Paper 应将此 framing 为 \"partial decomposition\n    that explains the transferable component and predicts method choice, but capability\n    residual remains confounded\"。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - title: Difficulty Probe Quality by Language (Qwen3 L48)\n    columns:\n    - lang\n    - tier\n    - difficulty_R2\n    - zs_transfer_R2\n    - delta\n    data:\n    - lang: en\n      tier: high\n      difficulty_R2: 0.71\n      zs_transfer_R2: null\n      delta: null\n    - lang: zh\n      tier: high\n      difficulty_R2: null\n      zs_transfer_R2: 0.67\n      delta: -0.04\n    - lang: de\n      tier: high\n      difficulty_R2: null\n      zs_transfer_R2: 0.68\n      delta: -0.03\n    - lang: es\n      tier: high\n      difficulty_R2: null\n      zs_transfer_R2: 0.69\n      delta: -0.02\n    - lang: ar\n      tier: mid\n      difficulty_R2: null\n      zs_transfer_R2: 0.63\n      delta: -0.08\n    - lang: hi\n      tier: mid\n      difficulty_R2: null\n      zs_transfer_R2: 0.61\n      delta: -0.1\n    - lang: ko\n      tier: mid\n      difficulty_R2: null\n      zs_transfer_R2: 0.6\n      delta: -0.11\n    - lang: vi\n      tier: mid\n      difficulty_R2: null\n      zs_transfer_R2: 0.58\n      delta: -0.13\n    - lang: sw\n      tier: low\n      difficulty_R2: null\n      zs_transfer_R2: 0.49\n      delta: -0.22\n    - lang: te\n      tier: low\n      difficulty_R2: null\n      zs_transfer_R2: 0.51\n      delta: -0.2\n  - title: Decomposition Effect on Transfer Gap (Qwen3, 8 layers averaged)\n    columns:\n    - component\n    - en_auroc\n    - zs_transfer_mean_9lang\n    - gap_pp\n    data:\n    - component: original correctness probe\n      en_auroc: 0.796\n      zs_transfer_mean_9lang: 0.674\n      gap_pp: 12.2\n    - component: difficulty probe only\n      en_auroc: 0.714\n      zs_transfer_mean_9lang: 0.67\n      gap_pp: 4.4\n    - component: residual (capability) probe\n      en_auroc: 0.758\n      zs_transfer_mean_9lang: 0.653\n      gap_pp: 10.5\n    - component: difficulty + residual reconstructed\n      en_auroc: 0.791\n      zs_transfer_mean_9lang: 0.671\n      gap_pp: 12.0\n  - title: Variance Decomposition by Layer Depth (Qwen3)\n    columns:\n    - layer\n    - difficulty_var_pct\n    - capability_var_pct\n    - reconstruction_loss_pct\n    data:\n    - layer: L20\n      difficulty_var_pct: 44\n      capability_var_pct: 51\n      reconstruction_loss_pct: 5\n    - layer: L28\n      difficulty_var_pct: 42\n      capability_var_pct: 53\n      reconstruction_loss_pct: 5\n    - layer: L36\n      difficulty_var_pct: 40\n      capability_var_pct: 54\n      reconstruction_loss_pct: 6\n    - layer: L48\n      difficulty_var_pct: 37\n      capability_var_pct: 56\n      reconstruction_loss_pct: 7\n    - layer: L56\n      difficulty_var_pct: 34\n      capability_var_pct: 58\n      reconstruction_loss_pct: 8\n    - layer: L64\n      difficulty_var_pct: 31\n      capability_var_pct: 60\n      reconstruction_loss_pct: 9\n    - layer: L76\n      difficulty_var_pct: 28\n      capability_var_pct: 62\n      reconstruction_loss_pct: 10\n    - layer: L84\n      difficulty_var_pct: 26\n      capability_var_pct: 63\n      reconstruction_loss_pct: 11\n  - title: 'Prescriptive Accuracy: Does Decomposition Predict Method Choice?'\n    note: For each lang-layer pair, decomposition predicts 'zero-shot suffices' if\n      difficulty component dominates (>50%), else 'CaCLR needed'. Ground truth from\n      plan_003.\n    columns:\n    - tier\n    - n_pairs\n    - correct_predictions\n    - accuracy\n    data:\n    - tier: high\n      n_pairs: 48\n      correct_predictions: 38\n      accuracy: 0.79\n    - tier: mid\n      n_pairs: 64\n      correct_predictions: 47\n      accuracy: 0.73\n    - tier: low\n      n_pairs: 40\n      correct_predictions: 25\n      accuracy: 0.63\n    - tier: all\n      n_pairs: 152\n      correct_predictions: 110\n      accuracy: 0.72\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Figure 4a: Stacked bar chart — per layer, the proportion of correctness direction\n    variance attributed to difficulty (blue), capability (orange), reconstruction\n    loss (grey). Difficulty share monotonically decreases from 44% at L20 to 26% at\n    L84; capability share correspondingly increases. Visual narrative: deeper layers\n    have more capability-specific information, which is why they transfer worse.\n\n    '\n  - 'Figure 4b: Scatter — x-axis: difficulty variance share (%), y-axis: zero-shot\n    transfer AUROC for each language-layer pair. Positive correlation (r≈0.55): higher\n    difficulty share predicts better zero-shot transfer. But substantial scatter,\n    especially for low-resource languages (marked with different symbol). Regression\n    line shown with confidence band.\n\n    '\n  analysis: 'Decomposition 部分成功：difficulty component 确实是 transferable part，其 share\n    随 depth 递减完美解释了 Pareto tradeoff 的机制——deeper layers 积累更多 capability-specific 信息，这些信息是\n    language-dependent 的。但 \"partial\" 体现在两方面：(1) difficulty 仅解释 37% 的 variance，多数 correctness\n    signal 在 capability residual 中；(2) capability residual 本身不是干净的 language-specific\n    signal，而是与 language-family effects confounded（IE 语言 cluster 说明 capability 共享有\n    phylogenetic 结构）。 Prescriptive accuracy 72% 是一个有用但不完美的 practical tool。Paper 应将此\n    framed 为 \"first decomposition of cross-lingual correctness transfer that identifies\n    the transferable component and partially predicts method choice, with the capability\n    residual as a target for future work.\"\n\n    '\n- name: Cross-Lingual Orthogonality Analysis\n  plan_id: plan_005\n  description: 'Extract verbalized confidence direction (prompt for P(correct) score,\n    fit linear probe), compute cosine similarity with correctness direction across\n    20 languages × 2 architectures. Resource-tier and language-family analysis.\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    cosine_mean_all: 0.091\n    cosine_mean_qwen3: 0.086\n    cosine_mean_llama4: 0.096\n    cosine_high_mean: 0.059\n    cosine_mid_mean: 0.084\n    cosine_low_mean: 0.147\n    cosine_low_std: 0.032\n    cosine_range:\n    - 0.04\n    - 0.21\n    en_cosine_qwen3: 0.04\n    en_cosine_llama4: 0.05\n    cross_arch_cosine_corr: 0.78\n    orthogonality_holds_all_20: true\n  result_rationale: 'Miao & Ungar (2026) 在英语 7-8B 模型上发现 correctness-confidence cosine\n    < 0.04。 在 median 档，该 orthogonality 跨语言泛化但有 resource-tier 梯度。High-resource 语言（cosine\n    ~0.06）接近英语水平，因为模型在这些语言上有充足的训练数据， verbalized confidence 和 internal correctness\n    的分离是 well-learned 的。 Mid-resource 语言（cosine ~0.08）稍高，模型的 confidence 表达在这些语言上 不那么\n    calibrated。Low-resource 语言（cosine ~0.15, std 0.032）明显更高且 variance 更大——模型在低资源语言上的\n    verbalized confidence 方向本身就不稳定（probe 拟合 noisy），导致与 correctness 的 cosine 更大也更不可靠。但即使最高的\n    yo (0.21) 也远低于 \"parallel\" 的 0.7+，orthogonality 的定性结论在所有 20 语言上成立。 Cross-architecture\n    correlation 0.78 表明 per-language cosine 值在两个模型上高度 一致——这是 structural property，不是\n    model-specific artifact。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - title: Correctness-Confidence Cosine Similarity by Language\n    columns:\n    - lang\n    - tier\n    - qwen3_cosine\n    - llama4_cosine\n    - mean\n    data:\n    - lang: en\n      tier: high\n      qwen3_cosine: 0.04\n      llama4_cosine: 0.05\n      mean: 0.045\n    - lang: zh\n      tier: high\n      qwen3_cosine: 0.05\n      llama4_cosine: 0.06\n      mean: 0.055\n    - lang: de\n      tier: high\n      qwen3_cosine: 0.06\n      llama4_cosine: 0.07\n      mean: 0.065\n    - lang: fr\n      tier: high\n      qwen3_cosine: 0.05\n      llama4_cosine: 0.06\n      mean: 0.055\n    - lang: es\n      tier: high\n      qwen3_cosine: 0.05\n      llama4_cosine: 0.06\n      mean: 0.055\n    - lang: ja\n      tier: high\n      qwen3_cosine: 0.07\n      llama4_cosine: 0.08\n      mean: 0.075\n    - lang: ru\n      tier: high\n      qwen3_cosine: 0.06\n      llama4_cosine: 0.07\n      mean: 0.065\n    - lang: ar\n      tier: mid\n      qwen3_cosine: 0.08\n      llama4_cosine: 0.09\n      mean: 0.085\n    - lang: hi\n      tier: mid\n      qwen3_cosine: 0.07\n      llama4_cosine: 0.08\n      mean: 0.075\n    - lang: ko\n      tier: mid\n      qwen3_cosine: 0.08\n      llama4_cosine: 0.09\n      mean: 0.085\n    - lang: pt\n      tier: mid\n      qwen3_cosine: 0.06\n      llama4_cosine: 0.07\n      mean: 0.065\n    - lang: vi\n      tier: mid\n      qwen3_cosine: 0.09\n      llama4_cosine: 0.1\n      mean: 0.095\n    - lang: th\n      tier: mid\n      qwen3_cosine: 0.1\n      llama4_cosine: 0.11\n      mean: 0.105\n    - lang: tr\n      tier: mid\n      qwen3_cosine: 0.08\n      llama4_cosine: 0.09\n      mean: 0.085\n    - lang: pl\n      tier: mid\n      qwen3_cosine: 0.07\n      llama4_cosine: 0.08\n      mean: 0.075\n    - lang: sw\n      tier: low\n      qwen3_cosine: 0.12\n      llama4_cosine: 0.13\n      mean: 0.125\n    - lang: te\n      tier: low\n      qwen3_cosine: 0.1\n      llama4_cosine: 0.11\n      mean: 0.105\n    - lang: my\n      tier: low\n      qwen3_cosine: 0.15\n      llama4_cosine: 0.16\n      mean: 0.155\n    - lang: am\n      tier: low\n      qwen3_cosine: 0.16\n      llama4_cosine: 0.17\n      mean: 0.165\n    - lang: yo\n      tier: low\n      qwen3_cosine: 0.18\n      llama4_cosine: 0.19\n      mean: 0.185\n  - title: Orthogonality Summary by Resource Tier\n    columns:\n    - tier\n    - n_langs\n    - cosine_mean\n    - cosine_std\n    - cosine_min\n    - cosine_max\n    data:\n    - tier: high\n      n_langs: 7\n      cosine_mean: 0.059\n      cosine_std: 0.01\n      cosine_min: 0.04\n      cosine_max: 0.08\n    - tier: mid\n      n_langs: 8\n      cosine_mean: 0.084\n      cosine_std: 0.013\n      cosine_min: 0.06\n      cosine_max: 0.11\n    - tier: low\n      n_langs: 5\n      cosine_mean: 0.147\n      cosine_std: 0.032\n      cosine_min: 0.1\n      cosine_max: 0.19\n    - tier: all\n      n_langs: 20\n      cosine_mean: 0.091\n      cosine_std: 0.04\n      cosine_min: 0.04\n      cosine_max: 0.19\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Figure 5: Dot plot — x-axis: cosine similarity, y-axis: languages (sorted by\n    resource tier, then by cosine). Two markers per language (circle=Qwen3, triangle=Llama4).\n    Vertical dashed line at cosine=0.25 (\"orthogonality threshold\"). All points to\n    the left. Clear visual gradient from high-resource (clustered near 0.05) to low-resource\n    (spread between 0.10-0.19). Error bars show bootstrap 95% CI. Annotation: \"Miao\n    & Ungar EN baseline: cos < 0.04\" with arrow pointing to English dots.\n\n    '\n  analysis: 'Claim 4 在 median 档下获得 strong support for high/mid-resource languages,\n    qualified support for low-resource。核心结论：correctness-confidence orthogonality 是一个跨语言\n    的 structural property，不是英语特有的。但 resource-tier gradient（high 0.06 → low 0.15） 表明该\n    property 在低资源语言上更弱——这可能是因为模型在低资源语言上的 confidence calibration 本身就差，confidence direction\n    拟合不稳定。Cross-architecture 一致性 0.78 进一步强化了 structural claim。Paper 应呈现为 \"orthogonality\n    universally holds (all cos < 0.25) but varies in degree, with implications for\n    why output-based calibration is structurally limited across all languages — but\n    especially limited for high-resource languages where the orthogonality is strongest.\"\n\n    '\n- name: Probe Complexity Comparison\n  plan_id: plan_006\n  description: 'Logistic regression vs 2-layer MLP (hidden dim 256, ReLU) at each\n    probed layer for both models. Compare English accuracy, cross-lingual transfer\n    degradation, and calibration quality. Test hypothesis: linear probes transfer\n    better.\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    qwen3_L76_logreg_en_auroc: 0.812\n    qwen3_L76_mlp_en_auroc: 0.827\n    qwen3_L76_logreg_transfer_mean: 0.644\n    qwen3_L76_mlp_transfer_mean: 0.607\n    qwen3_L76_logreg_transfer_drop_pp: 16.8\n    qwen3_L76_mlp_transfer_drop_pp: 22.0\n    llama4_L44_logreg_en_auroc: 0.793\n    llama4_L44_mlp_en_auroc: 0.812\n    llama4_L44_logreg_transfer_mean: 0.657\n    llama4_L44_mlp_transfer_mean: 0.625\n    llama4_L44_logreg_transfer_drop_pp: 13.6\n    llama4_L44_mlp_transfer_drop_pp: 18.7\n    mlp_en_advantage_pp_mean: 1.7\n    logreg_transfer_advantage_pp_mean: 3.5\n    hypothesis_confirmed: true\n  result_rationale: 'MLP 在英语上多 ~1.7pp AUROC，因为非线性层可以捕获 correctness 与 activation 之间\n    的非线性关系。但 MLP 在跨语言迁移上劣 ~3.5pp，因为非线性决策边界更容易 overfit 英语 activation 的分布特征，这些特征在其他语言中不保持。Linear\n    probe 的决策 超平面在 high-dimensional space 中更 \"blunt\"，因此更 robust to distribution shift。\n    这个结果与 Civelli et al. 的发现一致（linear > nonlinear for cross-lingual difficulty transfer），也回应了\n    reviewer 可能提出的 \"为什么不用更复杂的 probe\" 的质疑。 Paper 据此使用 logistic regression 作为 primary\n    probe，MLP 仅作为 ablation 报告。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - title: LogReg vs MLP at Key Layers (Qwen3-235B)\n    columns:\n    - layer\n    - logreg_en\n    - mlp_en\n    - en_delta\n    - logreg_transfer\n    - mlp_transfer\n    - transfer_delta\n    data:\n    - layer: L40\n      logreg_en: 0.776\n      mlp_en: 0.794\n      en_delta: 1.8\n      logreg_transfer: 0.696\n      mlp_transfer: 0.672\n      transfer_delta: -2.4\n    - layer: L52\n      logreg_en: 0.796\n      mlp_en: 0.813\n      en_delta: 1.7\n      logreg_transfer: 0.682\n      mlp_transfer: 0.651\n      transfer_delta: -3.1\n    - layer: L64\n      logreg_en: 0.807\n      mlp_en: 0.824\n      en_delta: 1.7\n      logreg_transfer: 0.661\n      mlp_transfer: 0.626\n      transfer_delta: -3.5\n    - layer: L76\n      logreg_en: 0.812\n      mlp_en: 0.827\n      en_delta: 1.5\n      logreg_transfer: 0.644\n      mlp_transfer: 0.607\n      transfer_delta: -3.7\n  - title: LogReg vs MLP at Key Layers (Llama 4 Scout)\n    columns:\n    - layer\n    - logreg_en\n    - mlp_en\n    - en_delta\n    - logreg_transfer\n    - mlp_transfer\n    - transfer_delta\n    data:\n    - layer: L24\n      logreg_en: 0.741\n      mlp_en: 0.758\n      en_delta: 1.7\n      logreg_transfer: 0.677\n      mlp_transfer: 0.654\n      transfer_delta: -2.3\n    - layer: L32\n      logreg_en: 0.771\n      mlp_en: 0.789\n      en_delta: 1.8\n      logreg_transfer: 0.679\n      mlp_transfer: 0.651\n      transfer_delta: -2.8\n    - layer: L40\n      logreg_en: 0.79\n      mlp_en: 0.808\n      en_delta: 1.8\n      logreg_transfer: 0.663\n      mlp_transfer: 0.631\n      transfer_delta: -3.2\n    - layer: L44\n      logreg_en: 0.793\n      mlp_en: 0.812\n      en_delta: 1.9\n      logreg_transfer: 0.657\n      mlp_transfer: 0.625\n      transfer_delta: -3.2\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Figure S1 (Appendix): Dual-line plot per model — x-axis: layer depth, y-axis:\n    AUROC. Solid lines = LogReg (blue = English, orange = transfer mean). Dashed lines\n    = MLP (blue = English, orange = transfer mean). The \"scissors\" pattern: MLP blue\n    line is above LogReg blue line (better English), but MLP orange line is below\n    LogReg orange line (worse transfer). Gap widens at deeper layers.\n\n    '\n  analysis: 'Hypothesis confirmed: linear probes transfer significantly better cross-lingually\n    than MLP probes (+3.5pp average), while sacrificing only 1.7pp English accuracy.\n    The transfer advantage of linear probes is larger at deeper layers (where distribution\n    shift is worst), which is consistent with the Pareto tradeoff mechanism — nonlinear\n    probes amplify the depth-dependent distribution shift. This result justifies the\n    methodological choice of logistic regression as the primary probe throughout the\n    paper.\n\n    '\n- name: Additional Benchmark Evaluation\n  plan_id: plan_007\n  description: 'Evaluate best probes + CaCLR on Belebele (20 languages, reading comprehension)\n    and MMLU-ProX (20 languages, harder STEM questions). Tests generalization of Pareto\n    frontier and CaCLR beyond GlobalMMLU.\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    belebele_en_auroc_best: 0.798\n    belebele_zs_transfer_mean_at_best_transfer: 0.708\n    belebele_pareto_replicates: true\n    belebele_caclr_vs_linproj_pp: 1.1\n    belebele_best_transfer_layer_qwen3: L44\n    mmlupx_en_auroc_best: 0.824\n    mmlupx_zs_transfer_mean_at_best_transfer: 0.681\n    mmlupx_pareto_replicates: true\n    mmlupx_caclr_vs_linproj_pp: 1.6\n    mmlupx_best_transfer_layer_qwen3: L40\n    belebele_low_resource_pass_rate: 0.6\n    mmlupx_low_resource_pass_rate: 0.4\n  result_rationale: 'Pareto frontier 作为 representation structure 的 property，不应依赖特定\n    benchmark。 Belebele（阅读理解）和 MMLU-ProX（更难 STEM 题）提供了两个不同难度和认知类型的 测试。Belebele 稍简单，英语\n    AUROC 稍低（0.798 vs 0.812）因为 reading comprehension 的 correctness 比 knowledge QA\n    更依赖 surface patterns，linear probe 的 ceiling 更低。 但迁移质量稍高（0.708 vs 0.696）因为阅读理解的跨语言\n    pattern 更相似。MMLU-ProX 更难，英语 AUROC 更高（0.824）因为难题的 correctness signal 更 salient（模型更\n    \"确定\" 自己是否知道），但迁移稍差（0.681）因为 STEM 知识的跨语言 variation 更大。 CaCLR 在 MMLU-ProX 上优势稍大（+1.6pp\n    vs +1.1pp）因为更难的题目有更多 distribution shift 可以被 consistency term 修正。两个 benchmark 都复现了\n    Pareto 结构，确认其 generalizability。低资源在 MMLU-ProX 上更差（2/5 vs 3/5）因为难题放大了数据不足的问题。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - title: Cross-Benchmark Comparison (Qwen3-235B, LogReg)\n    columns:\n    - metric\n    - GlobalMMLU\n    - Belebele\n    - MMLU_ProX\n    data:\n    - metric: en_auroc_best\n      GlobalMMLU: 0.812\n      Belebele: 0.798\n      MMLU_ProX: 0.824\n    - metric: best_en_layer\n      GlobalMMLU: L76\n      Belebele: L72\n      MMLU_ProX: L76\n    - metric: best_transfer_layer\n      GlobalMMLU: L40\n      Belebele: L44\n      MMLU_ProX: L40\n    - metric: zs_transfer_mean\n      GlobalMMLU: 0.696\n      Belebele: 0.708\n      MMLU_ProX: 0.681\n    - metric: transfer_drop_pp\n      GlobalMMLU: 16.8\n      Belebele: 13.1\n      MMLU_ProX: 18.4\n    - metric: caclr_vs_linproj_pp\n      GlobalMMLU: 1.4\n      Belebele: 1.1\n      MMLU_ProX: 1.6\n    - metric: low_resource_pass_rate\n      GlobalMMLU: 0.6\n      Belebele: 0.6\n      MMLU_ProX: 0.4\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Figure S2 (Appendix): Three-panel Pareto frontier plots (GlobalMMLU / Belebele\n    / MMLU-ProX) with identical axis scales. Visual pattern clearly replicates across\n    all three: upward-then-left curve in all panels, with MMLU-ProX showing the steepest\n    tradeoff and Belebele the mildest.\n\n    '\n  analysis: 'Cross-benchmark replication is the key result: Pareto frontier structure\n    is benchmark- agnostic, confirming it reflects model representation properties\n    rather than dataset artifacts. The quantitative differences (Belebele flatter,\n    MMLU-ProX steeper) are interpretable and strengthen the paper''s analysis. CaCLR''s\n    benchmark-robust improvement (+1.1 to +1.6pp) confirms its general utility.\n\n    '\n- name: INT8 Validation Ablation\n  plan_id: plan_010\n  description: 'Compare INT8 vs FP16 probing results at 5 representative layers for\n    Llama 4 Scout on 5% random subset (~700 samples). Validates that INT8 quantization\n    doesn''t distort correctness signals in the activation space.\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    max_auroc_delta_pp: 0.3\n    mean_auroc_delta_pp: 0.24\n    direction_bias: negligible (INT8 marginally lower at all layers)\n    cosine_sim_directions: 0.997\n    conclusion: INT8 validated — no meaningful distortion of correctness signal\n  result_rationale: 'INT8 weight-only quantization 保留了 activation space 的大部分结构（weight\n    quantization 引入的 perturbation 在 high-dimensional space 中被分摊，对线性 probe 的影响极小）。\n    AUROC delta < 0.3pp 远低于实验中观测到的其他 effect sizes（transfer drop 13-17pp, CaCLR improvement\n    1-4pp）。Correctness direction 的 cosine similarity 0.997 说明 quantization 几乎不改变 direction，只是\n    slightly perturb magnitude。这是 expected result，但对 reviewer 来说是必要的 due diligence——没有这个\n    ablation，reviewer 可能质疑 INT8 是否引入 systematic bias。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - title: INT8 vs FP16 Probing Results (Llama 4 Scout, 5% subset)\n    columns:\n    - layer\n    - int8_auroc\n    - fp16_auroc\n    - delta_pp\n    - direction_cosine\n    data:\n    - layer: L4\n      int8_auroc: 0.568\n      fp16_auroc: 0.571\n      delta_pp: -0.3\n      direction_cosine: 0.998\n    - layer: L12\n      int8_auroc: 0.648\n      fp16_auroc: 0.651\n      delta_pp: -0.3\n      direction_cosine: 0.997\n    - layer: L24\n      int8_auroc: 0.738\n      fp16_auroc: 0.74\n      delta_pp: -0.2\n      direction_cosine: 0.998\n    - layer: L36\n      int8_auroc: 0.78\n      fp16_auroc: 0.782\n      delta_pp: -0.2\n      direction_cosine: 0.997\n    - layer: L44\n      int8_auroc: 0.791\n      fp16_auroc: 0.794\n      delta_pp: -0.3\n      direction_cosine: 0.996\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Figure S3 (Appendix): Paired bar chart — 5 layers, INT8 (blue) vs FP16 (orange)\n    bars. Bars nearly identical height at every layer. Annotation: \"max Δ = 0.3pp\".\n    Simple, clean validation figure.\n\n    '\n  analysis: 'INT8 quantization is validated for correctness probing. The <0.3pp AUROC\n    difference is well within noise levels and has no systematic direction. This ablation\n    can be reported in 2-3 sentences in the Appendix with the table — no need for\n    extended discussion.\n\n    '\n- name: Gemma 4 31B Dense — Camera-Ready Extension\n  plan_id: plan_008\n  description: 'Third architecture (60 layers, dense, FP16) for camera-ready version.\n    Dense vs MoE architectural contrast. Full Pareto frontier, 20+ languages.\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    en_auroc_best: 0.805\n    en_best_layer: L48\n    best_transfer_layer: L32\n    zs_transfer_mean_at_best_transfer: 0.709\n    zs_transfer_drop_at_best_en_pp: 10.2\n    pareto_frontier_shape: smoother than MoE models, more gradual transfer decline\n    low_resource_pass_rate: 0.6\n    caclr_vs_linproj_pp: 1.0\n    frontier_agreement_with_qwen3: 0.62\n    frontier_agreement_with_llama4: 0.71\n  result_rationale: 'Dense architecture 与 MoE 的关键差异：没有 routing 机制导致的 discrete layer-wise\n    变化，representation 的 language-specificity 随 depth 更连续地增长。因此 Pareto frontier 更 smooth（transfer\n    decline 更 gradual），transfer drop 仅 10.2pp（vs Qwen3 16.8pp, Llama4 13.6pp）。English\n    AUROC 略低于 Qwen3（0.805 vs 0.812）因为 31B dense 的 total compute 少于 235B MoE。Best transfer\n    在 53% 深度（L32/60）， 介于 Qwen3(43%) 和 Llama4(67%) 之间。CaCLR 优势更小（+1.0pp）因为 dense model\n    的 representation shift across languages 本身更 gradual，simple baselines 已经 表现不错。与\n    Llama4 的 frontier agreement (0.71) 高于与 Qwen3 (0.62)，可能因为 Llama4 和 Gemma4 的训练数据组成更相似。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - title: Three-Architecture Pareto Summary\n    columns:\n    - metric\n    - Qwen3_235B_MoE\n    - Llama4_Scout_MoE\n    - Gemma4_31B_Dense\n    data:\n    - metric: total_layers\n      Qwen3_235B_MoE: 94\n      Llama4_Scout_MoE: 48\n      Gemma4_31B_Dense: 60\n    - metric: architecture\n      Qwen3_235B_MoE: MoE\n      Llama4_Scout_MoE: MoE\n      Gemma4_31B_Dense: Dense\n    - metric: en_auroc_best\n      Qwen3_235B_MoE: 0.812\n      Llama4_Scout_MoE: 0.793\n      Gemma4_31B_Dense: 0.805\n    - metric: best_transfer_depth_pct\n      Qwen3_235B_MoE: 43\n      Llama4_Scout_MoE: 67\n      Gemma4_31B_Dense: 53\n    - metric: transfer_drop_pp\n      Qwen3_235B_MoE: 16.8\n      Llama4_Scout_MoE: 13.6\n      Gemma4_31B_Dense: 10.2\n    - metric: frontier_smoothness\n      Qwen3_235B_MoE: sharp\n      Llama4_Scout_MoE: flat/noisy\n      Gemma4_31B_Dense: smooth\n    - metric: caclr_benefit_pp\n      Qwen3_235B_MoE: 1.4\n      Llama4_Scout_MoE: 1.2\n      Gemma4_31B_Dense: 1.0\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Figure 6 (Camera-Ready): Three-model overlaid Pareto frontiers. Qwen3 (circles)\n    shows widest, steepest frontier. Llama4 (triangles) shows compact, flat frontier.\n    Gemma4 (squares) shows smooth, intermediate frontier. Visual immediately communicates\n    architecture-dependent Pareto structure. Inset table shows optimal transfer depth\n    %.\n\n    '\n  analysis: 'Dense vs MoE 对比是 camera-ready 的最有价值的扩展。Dense 架构的 smoother frontier 提供了\n    mechanistic insight：MoE routing 在深层的 language-specific expert selection 可能是 Qwen3\n    sharp Pareto tradeoff 的原因，而 dense model 的 continuous feature evolution 产生更 gradual\n    的 language specificity 增长。三架构的 frontier 定性一致 但定量不同，强化了 \"Pareto frontier is universal\n    but architecture-dependent\" 的 headline claim。\n\n    '\n- name: Extended Language Coverage — Camera-Ready Extension\n  plan_id: plan_009\n  description: 'Expand from 20 to 50+ languages using GlobalMMLU/Belebele full language\n    sets. Tests how Pareto frontier patterns scale to long-tail languages.\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    total_languages: 53\n    high_resource_count: 12\n    mid_resource_count: 18\n    low_resource_count: 23\n    zs_transfer_mean_all_52: 0.651\n    low_resource_pass_rate_23: 0.35\n    very_low_resource_auroc_range:\n    - 0.5\n    - 0.58\n    pareto_replicates_qualitatively: true\n    new_failure_languages:\n    - qu\n    - ha\n    - gn\n    - lg\n    - ny\n    - sn\n    - xh\n    - zu\n    - ig\n    - mg\n    - rw\n    - so\n    - tn\n    - ts\n    - ve\n    caclr_improvement_rate_52: 0.67\n    layer_rank_consistency_52: 0.58\n  result_rationale: '扩展到 53 语言后，低资源尾部显著增长（23 个 low-resource vs 原来 5 个），整体 指标下降是 expected\n    的。ZS transfer mean 从 0.696（20 langs）降至 0.651（52 non-en langs）因为新增语言大部分是低资源的非洲/大洋洲/美洲原住民语言，GlobalMMLU\n    翻译 质量参差不齐。低资源 pass rate 从 0.6（3/5）降至 0.35（8/23）说明 \"correctness direction universally\n    transfers\" 的说法在尾部语言不成立——但 Pareto 结构本身 仍然定性存在。CaCLR 的 improvement rate 也从 0.74\n    降至 0.67，但仍是多数语言 受益。Layer ranking consistency 从 0.71 降至 0.58，因为低资源语言的最优迁移层 更分散。Paper\n    应将此 framing 为 \"Pareto frontier scales to 50+ languages but with diminishing returns\n    for very low-resource languages, motivating future work on low-resource-specific\n    transfer methods.\"\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - title: Extended Coverage Summary by Tier\n    columns:\n    - tier\n    - n_langs_20\n    - n_langs_53\n    - mean_auroc_20\n    - mean_auroc_53\n    - pass_rate_20\n    - pass_rate_53\n    data:\n    - tier: high\n      n_langs_20: 6\n      n_langs_53: 11\n      mean_auroc_20: 0.753\n      mean_auroc_53: 0.745\n      pass_rate_20: 1.0\n      pass_rate_53: 1.0\n    - tier: mid\n      n_langs_20: 8\n      n_langs_53: 18\n      mean_auroc_20: 0.711\n      mean_auroc_53: 0.698\n      pass_rate_20: 1.0\n      pass_rate_53: 0.94\n    - tier: low\n      n_langs_20: 5\n      n_langs_53: 23\n      mean_auroc_20: 0.607\n      mean_auroc_53: 0.571\n      pass_rate_20: 0.6\n      pass_rate_53: 0.35\n    - tier: all\n      n_langs_20: 19\n      n_langs_53: 52\n      mean_auroc_20: 0.696\n      mean_auroc_53: 0.651\n      pass_rate_20: 0.89\n      pass_rate_53: 0.69\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Figure 7 (Camera-Ready): Language-level scatter — x-axis: log(pretraining data\n    size estimate, tokens), y-axis: best zero-shot transfer AUROC. Clear positive\n    correlation (r≈0.72). Horizontal dashed line at AUROC=0.60. Labels for notable\n    languages. Below the line: cluster of 15 very-low-resource languages. Color by\n    language family. Shows that transfer success is primarily a function of pretraining\n    representation quality.\n\n    '\n  analysis: 'Extended coverage confirms the fundamental insight: Pareto frontier is\n    a structural property that scales to 50+ languages, but the practical utility\n    of zero-shot correctness probe transfer is bounded by pretraining data quantity.\n    The 15 languages below the 0.60 threshold are all in the lowest quintile of pretraining\n    data, suggesting a minimum representation quality floor for this approach. This\n    limitation should be acknowledged transparently in the Discussion section, not\n    hidden — it''s a valuable finding about the scope of probe-based calibration methods.'\n","numLines":1672,"startLine":1,"totalLines":1672}}}
